    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0eb4d543_0fd46195",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T17:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Completion of the MMU disable only needs an ISB. The important thing here is to ensure is that whatever we are executing afterwards (fw code as well as payload code) is cleaned from the caches to the point of coherency (PoC) as subsequent instruction fetches won\u0027t hit in unified caches between PoU and PoC.",
      "parentUuid": "6a875065_2c290d65",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "864e5d50_a4d36868",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-25T14:36:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a problem if previous writes have not completed before the MMU and cache are disabled?",
      "parentUuid": "0eb4d543_0fd46195",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "faf2f976_9f93f814",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-26T14:58:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to the question above.\n\n\u003e as subsequent instruction fetches won\u0027t hit in unified caches between PoU and PoC.\n\nI might be missing something but is this relevant here, given that we execute in-place (both the \"loader\" (which actually doesn\u0027t load anything) and its payload) from memory pre-loaded by the VMM or HV? From the PoV of the VM, it\u0027s as if the DDR came preloaded with executable code, right?",
      "parentUuid": "864e5d50_a4d36868",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c5e6b55_bb15b5a5",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-27T13:29:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027Completion\u0027 of a store is usually defined in terms of observability by other agents, but this is irrelevant here. What is relevant is that the store is issued before disabling the MMU in program order, and so the store either faults synchronously if no mapping exists, or it succeeds, and disabling the MMU has no effect on it. Whether/when other CPUs might be able to observe the store in memory is a separate question.\n\nAs for the payload: if it is guaranteed to be clean to the PoC in memory already, then no D-cache maintenance is needed, but I-cache invalidation might be. I guess putting the assumptions/guarantees in a comment here would be helpful",
      "parentUuid": "864e5d50_a4d36868",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56267a4a_e4881d7d",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-06T15:11:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So do we need a DSB or not in the end? I guess even apart from the MMU, we might want at least one to assume that any stores which are clearing secrets from memory are guaranteed to be observed by all cores, in case case the payload starts other cores?",
      "parentUuid": "6c5e6b55_bb15b5a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "346c6b24_bd8c5fda",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T12:41:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no point in managing concurrent wrt cores that are not even up yet. Please just drop the DSB unless it serves a particular purpose.",
      "parentUuid": "56267a4a_e4881d7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff34458c_2e0f4d3f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-11T10:48:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That feels a bit too drastic: can\u0027t we simply flip the bits we don\u0027t want (`M` and `C`, I suppose)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad442083_d4bb23e1",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T16:54:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seemed best to put it in a known state; won\u0027t the next stage U-Boot initialise it however it wants anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "ff34458c_2e0f4d3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5bee953_7ef46eeb",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T17:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It also violates the architecture, as there are RES1 fields in some of those registers as well, and SCTLR_ELx has fields that have nothing to do with translation.\n\nBetter to only clear the M bit if disabling the MMU is what you are after.",
      "parentUuid": "ff34458c_2e0f4d3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "557fac8f_8cedc62b",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-25T14:36:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like a good idea to also clear C, SA, I, WXN and other fields which are not RES1, so I\u0027ve changed this to zero everything except for the RES1 fields.",
      "parentUuid": "b5bee953_7ef46eeb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7601146_1494d8f7",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-27T13:29:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is that a good idea? In fact, keeping the I-cache enabled is preferred, as it doesn\u0027t rely on the MMU like the D-cache.",
      "parentUuid": "557fac8f_8cedc62b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a35c94bc_e6379900",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-06T15:11:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The payload might not want to enforce SP to be aligned, and in any case won\u0027t have working exception handlers initially, so having SA set to 0 seems safer.\n\nWe need to disable at least the data cache, right? And C is specified to be 0 on warm reset, so that seems like the correct value to reset it to here.\n\nThe payload may have writable code, so WXN needs to be 0 (though I guess it will set it as needed when setting up its page table anyway).",
      "parentUuid": "b7601146_1494d8f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93af8dbd_ca12c3cf",
        "filename": "pvmfw/payload.S",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T12:41:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The payload will do whatever it needs to do to put the CPU in the right mode. It doesn\u0027t make a lot of sense to try and anticipate it here.",
      "parentUuid": "a35c94bc_e6379900",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "6a4e59a4f95889be0c754563581b240eca5b7882",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
