      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T17:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the point of zeroing these registers. As Pierre-Clement points out, you shouldn\u0027t touch the registers that configure the translation before clearing the M bit has completed, so you at least need an ISB here. Clearing TCR and MAIR serves no real purpose, and clearing VBAR doesn\u0027t make that much sense either - if an exception is taken unexpectedly after this point, jumping to an arbitrary address that is unlikely to be covered by DRAM is not any better than jumping to the firmware\u0027s exception handler as long as it still there.",
